     "text": "{\"reachable\": false, \"rationale\": \"With mfa_admin deployed, auth_dc (which requires NOT mfa_admin) is blocked, and it is the only way to get foothold_dc. Without foothold_dc, escalate_dc cannot give admin_dc. Without admin_dc, dump_dbadmin_dc cannot give stolen_dbadmin, which is the only source of that credential. auth_db and auth_fileserver both require stolen_dbadmin, so foothold_db and foothold_fileserver are unreachable. That makes admin_db and admin_fileserver unreachable, so neither exfiltrate_db nor exfiltrate_fileserver can fire. The attacker can still reach the internal network, the appserver and stolen_admin (via phish, pivot, auth_appserver and kerberoast), but exfiltrated cannot become true.\"}"
